      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SUZYS DREAM (2) turned in a much better run at her latest appearance when she scored as the odds-on favourite by a neck over 1690m at Shepparton after having raced outside the leader at the bell. Will enjoy a nice run from this favourable starting position. Recent effort is good enough to win a race of this calibre. CHINSKI NZ (3) finished third last start, beaten 19 metres at Melton over 2240m when trying to lead all of the way. Expect him to pose a serious challenge. OUR TINKA BELLE (8) broke last start but still managed to fill a minor placing over 1609m at Geelong, finishing 1.1 metres from the winner. That was a pleasing progression after missing the placings the run before. No harm in drawing here with the sprint lane to rely upon. Meets a similar line up so she must be considered. JESSICAS STORY (9) disappointed last time when sixth over 1690m at this track. Can do a lot better so is worth considering.",
